  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Page No.# 1/3 vs The State Of Assam And Anr on 14 September, 2021 Author: Rumi Kumari Phukan Bench: Rumi Kumari Phukan Page No.# 1/3 Gahc010135022021 The Gauhati High Court (High Court Of Assam, Nagaland, Mizoram And Arunachal Pradesh) Case No. : Crl.Pet./449/2021 Ujjal Saha And Anr. S/O Sri Uttam Saha, C/O Adani Wilmar Limited, Hatigarh Warehouse, Charigaon Mouza, Dist-Jorhat, Assam, R/O Kaziranga Mercantiles, Mariani Road, Cinnamara Kathkhatia Gaon, Katani Mauza, Jorhat, P.O.-Duklangia, P.S.-Cinnamara, Pin-785634, Assam 2: Ashis Mitra S/O Sri S.K. Mitra C/O Adani Wilmar Limited Hatigarh Warehouse Charigaon Mouza Dist-Jorhat Assam R/O Chanditala Lane Regent Park P.O.-Regent Park P.S.-Regent Park Kolkat Versus The State Of Assam And Anr. Represented By The Public Prosecutor, Assam 2:Bibhuti Bhushan Das Food Safety Officer Golaghat And Jorhat District Assam. Represented By The Public Prosecutor Assa Page No.# 1/3 vs The State Of Assam And Anr on 14 September, 2021 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/47243210/ 1 Advocate for the Petitioner : Mr. A M Bora Advocate for the Respondent : Pp, Assam Page No.# 2/3 :: Before :: Hon'Ble Mrs. Justice Rumi Kumari Phukan Order",
    "facts": "By way of this petition under Section 482 read with Section 401 CrPC, the petitioners have sought for setting aside of the impugned order dated 16.07.2019 as well as the proceeding pertaining to Complaint Case No.161/2019 under Section 26(2)(i) & 27(2)(c) read with Section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 pending in the court of the learned Chief Judicial Magistrate, Jorhat on the ground that the present two petitioners were arrayed as accused in the offence report without including the company as an accused, for which the prosecution itself is bad in law. Also perused the complaint so filed, wherein it is reflected that the company in question has not been impleaded as a party to the case.",
